# UI copy and type

User-visible words use **Title Case**: the first letter of each word is capital. Do not set whole labels in ALL CAPITALS. Do not leave labels in sentence case.

## Copy

- Run headings, buttons, badges, nav, table headers, field labels, and empty states through `formatUiText()` in `apps/web/src/lib/formatUiText.ts`.
- `PageHeader`, `PageHero`, `Button`, and `Badge` already do this for string children. Pass the raw phrase.
- Keep real acronyms as written: RFI, QAP, BOQ, SPDC, GFC, DPR, NCR, CRM, HRMS.
- Do not add Tailwind `uppercase`, `tracking-wider` shout styles, or `text-transform: uppercase`.

```tsx
// Good
<Button>Save Draft</Button>
formatUiText("Select Package")

// Bad
<span className="uppercase">SAVE DRAFT</span>
<span>select package</span>
```

## Font

- The app face is **Arial** (`--font-sans`, `--font-display`, and `--font-mono` in `apps/web/src/index.css`).
- Do not introduce another Latin webfont for UI text.
- The Hindi word on the brand lockup (`.brand-lockup__hi`) stays in a Devanagari face. Arial does not cover that word.
